cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GLIDER: General Laboratory Interface for Design, Experimentation, and Recording"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "LaingLab"
    name-particle: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/LaingLab/glider"
url: "https://github.com/LaingLab/glider"
abstract: >-
  GLIDER is a visual-programming environment for designing, running, and
  recording behavioral and physiological experiments. It connects directly
  to Arduino, Raspberry Pi GPIO, I2C devices, USB cameras, and the UCLA
  Miniscope V4, producing synchronized CSV and video output suitable for
  scientific analysis.
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - behavior
  - electrophysiology
  - laboratory automation
  - data acquisition
  - miniscope
  - arduino
  - raspberry pi
